{"qid":"Q197598","names":["Zheng"],"title":"Zheng","endonym":null,"capsule":"The state of Zheng (郑/鄭) was founded c. 806 BCE as a Zhou royal appanage in present-day central Henan and rose to regional prominence in the Spring and Autumn period under Duke Zhuang (r. 743–701 BCE), who briefly dominated inter-state diplomacy and defied the Zhou king. Zheng's position between the more powerful states of Jin, Chu, and later Qi made it perpetually subject to coercion and alliance politics, and its territory shrank accordingly over the Warring States period. The state was conquered and extinguished by Han in 375 BCE after the fall of its last capital at Xinzheng.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Zheng's approximate territory in the central Yellow River plain is attested by the Zuo Zhuan and Shiji; detailed boundary maps are scholarly reconstructions with significant uncertainty, particularly for the late Warring States contraction.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Zheng (state)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zheng_(state)"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Duke Zhuang of Zheng","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_Zhuang_of_Zheng"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Spring and Autumn period","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_and_Autumn_period"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Han (state)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_(state)"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Zheng (state)","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Duke Zhuang of Zheng","nativeName":"鄭莊公","roman":"Zheng Zhuang Gong","start":-743,"end":-701,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Duke Zhao of Zheng","na